## 2026-08-12 — P4 alignment: meaningful L0↔L2 benchmark + baseline (this session)
Replaced the trivial by-construction gloss↔iast baseline with the real task. Per `docs/P4_ALIGNMENT_SPEC.md`,
P4 = recover the inline IAST anchors the L2 prose marks in parens and link each to its L0 lemma in the same
passage; abstain on non-anchored (SUPPLIED) prose. Built `pipeline/l0_align.py` + `pipeline/test_l0_align.py`
(22/22 pass). Floor: resolution recall 0.93, precision 0.89, abstain 1.0 over 35 passages / 105 anchors
(diacritic-aware IAST detection + stem-as-prefix / diacritic-insensitive matching per the P2 lesson).
awesome-align (not installed) must beat 0.93. Report: `docs/p4_alignment_eval_report.json`.

## 2026-08-12 — P4 independent witness (Vidyut) — non-human independence
Added the independent morphological witness to the P4 benchmark (no fresh human gold available). Rejected
awesome-align (sentence-level MT aligner, wrong granularity); adopted Vidyut (P2 engine, CPU) as the
independent second method. Result over 99 resolved links: AGREE 38 / DISAGREE 9 / UNABLE 52 →
agree_rate_analyzed_only 0.81. UNABLE = Vidyut can't parse inflected/compound L0 surfaces (honest
abstention). 9 DISAGREE are mostly Vidyut compound-analysis errors, not genuine mismatches. This
establishes independence the same way P2 did (multi-witness ensemble). 26/26 tests pass.

