## 2026-08-12 — V1 legacy extractor pass: IPVV L0 proof 35/63 → 63/63
Built `pipeline/extract_l0_v1.py` — the V1 (01_t1, Vol 1) legacy-prose → canonical L0 adapter. V1 is
continuous prose with inline `GLOSS (IAST)` (no `[and]-` markers), `[bracket]` connectives, line-wraps.
Design rule: every word becomes a token (gloss-word absorbs its `(IAST)`; bare words/brackets are
gloss-only tokens) → full coverage, no lettered gaps. Result: **the EXISTING verify_l0.py passes
UNCHANGED** (byte-identical to git) over V1: **28/28 PASS**, 91,714 tokens. Full IPVV now **63/63 P0**
(V2/V3 35/35 + V1 28/28). Added 3 adversarial fixtures (`tests/l0_v1/`) + `pipeline/test_extract_l0_v1.py`
(21/21 pass). Honest claim: 63/63 proves two-format robustness, NOT cross-work generalization (that
waits for a second real work). CLAIMS.md P-001 updated. verify_l0.py untouched.

